    <</button>>
:: GameIntro

    <span class='red'>CAUTION!</span>
    <em>There can be some dark moments in this game, especially with regards to your backstory. If you are uncomfortable with imagining a severe emotional and physical loss, then I kindly ask you find something else to play. But if you feel like being bold and accepting a difficult rebirth, then I would love for you to continue.</em>
    
    <hr>

    Welcome to Live Another Life! This quick page will introduce you to a few keys things before getting into the game.

    This is a game of choices, developement, advancement, and consequences set in modern day America. But most of all it is freedom. You have the freedom to choose who and what your character is.

    There is nothing physically stopping you from being a poisonious, decietful, and vindictive person. While you might not be able to make use of your friends to help you accomplish your goals, with enough studying and exploring you will still be able to succeed at whatever it is you seek.

    If you decide to focus soley on your relationships with others, they will be able to help you advance your abilities and offer you assistance quickly, but only up to the extent of their knowledge and experiences.

    There will be no immersion breaking explanations of mechanics or characters. You will learn as you go. Asking questions, reading books, studying tomes, and casting spells will all help you give you more complete understanding of how the world works and what you can do with.

    So go forth and Live Another Life!

    <<button [[Awesome | PersonalityTest]]>><</button>>

:: PersonalityTest
    Before you begin, please answer these questions to establish your starting your alter ego's personality. This will likely change as you make choices throughout your new life, but a baseline is needed! Please choose the most applicable answers:

    /*openn*/\
    Do you enjoy routines?
    <label><<radiobutton "$temP.o1" -50 checked>> Yes</label>
    <label><<radiobutton "$temP.o1" 0>> Eh, they're fine</label>
    <label><<radiobutton "$temP.o1" 50>> No</label>

    /*conscient*/\
    How organized are you?
    <label><<radiobutton "$temP.c1" 50 checked>> I'm pretty organized</label>
    <label><<radiobutton "$temP.c1" 0>> Average, I guess?</label>
    <label><<radiobutton "$temP.c1" -50>> Not at all</label>

    /*neurot*/\
    Do you bounce between different emotions?
    <label><<radiobutton "$temP.n1" 50 checked>> All the time!</label>
    <label><<radiobutton "$temP.n1" 0>> Sometimes?</label>
    <label><<radiobutton "$temP.n1" -50>> Not often at all</label>

    /*extrav*/\
    How much of your time is spent with friends?
    <label><<radiobutton "$temP.e1" 50 checked>> I love hanging with friends!</label>
    <label><<radiobutton "$temP.e1" 0>> Pretty often</label>
    <label><<radiobutton "$temP.e1" -50>> Friends? I don't know that word</label>

    /*openn*/\
    How much do you like to try new things?
    <label><<radiobutton "$temP.o2" 50 checked>> I love new things!</label>
    <label><<radiobutton "$temP.o2" 0>> More or less</label>
    <label><<radiobutton "$temP.o2" -50>> Not really</label>

    /*agreeb*/\
    Do you put your needs before others in life?
    <label><<radiobutton "$temP.a1" -50 checked>> Almost all the time</label>
    <label><<radiobutton "$temP.a1" 0>> Sometimes yes, sometimes no</label>
    <label><<radiobutton "$temP.a1" 50>> Rarely, if ever</label>

    /*extrav*/\
    How much energy do you regain when spending time with people?
    <label><<radiobutton "$temP.e2" 50 checked>> I feel like a new person!</label>
    <label><<radiobutton "$temP.e2" 0>> Not much</label>
    <label><<radiobutton "$temP.e2" -50>> Gain? I lose energy</label>

    /*agreeb*/\
    Do you like to debate with others?
    <label><<radiobutton "$temP.a2" -50 checked>> Whenever I can</label>
    <label><<radiobutton "$temP.a2" 0>> When I need to</label>
    <label><<radiobutton "$temP.a2" 50>> I hate it</label>

    /*neurot*/\
    How often do you get stressed out?
    <label><<radiobutton "$temP.n2" 50 checked>> Egh, pretty often</label>
    <label><<radiobutton "$temP.n2" 0>> No more than the next person</label>
    <label><<radiobutton "$temP.n2" -50>> Psh, almost never</label>

    /*conscient*/\
    How much willpower do you have?
    <label><<radiobutton "$temP.c2" 50 checked>> I can definitely control myself</label>
    <label><<radiobutton "$temP.c2" 0>> I give into temptation sometimes</label>
    <label><<radiobutton "$temP.c2" -50>> Oh, I cannot stop myself</label>

    <<button [[Ready! | Dream1]]>><</button>>
:: Dream1
    This will use the base mechanics of the game to give a taste of what's to come.

    <<button [[Skip...for now. | WakingUp1]]>><</button>>

:: WakingUp1
    <<nobr>>
    <<set $plrPersonality.openn = $plrPersonality.openn + $temP.o1 + $temP.o2>>
    <<set $plrPersonality.conscient = $plrPersonality.conscient + $temP.c1 + $temP.c2>>
    <<set $plrPersonality.neurot = $plrPersonality.neurot + $temP.n1 + $temP.n2>>
    <<set $plrPersonality.extrav = $plrPersonality.extrav + $temP.e1 + $temP.e2>>
    <<set $plrPersonality.agreeb = $plrPersonality.agreeb + $temP.a1 + $temP.a2>>
    <</nobr>>\
    <img src="img/medicalwing.jpg" alt="medical wing photo"/>

    You feel uneasy. Not yet able to make sense of it, you know something is strange. As you slowly wake up, you know you aren't anywhere you remember ever being before. The smell is unfamiliar. The bed you realize you are laying in, is different. Even the air feels different, thicker, maybe.

    You slowly open your eyes, feeling quite groggy and disoriented,

    The room is dimly lit, yet richly decorated. Full of reds and stained wood. And it's cavernous with high ceilings. The light is provided by numerous candles arranged on shelves and bedside tables. Come to think of it, there are a lot of beds here.

    And the candles... Well the candles look normal, but the flames are... Wrong. They are floating above the wicks!

    Before you're able to make sense of any of thing you are seeing, the large wooden doors to the room open. A woman wearing a white robe and hood is walking across the black marble floor and snacking on a bread roll. This is all so strange.

    She notices you are awake and says "Oh, I am so sorry!"

    <<button [[Continue | WakingUp2]]>><</button>>

:: WakingUp2
    <img src="img/medicalwing.jpg" alt="medical wing photo"/>

    "My name is $npcs.Amy.formal, I am the Medicus for this school."

    "Again I am so sorry I wasn't here when you woke up. I am sure you are confused with your situation."

    "Unfortunately, its not my place to explain what's going on, you'll have to speak with Headmaster Donaver. As soon as I'm done making sure you are in decent shape, I will have someone take you to him. So I don't mean to be rude, but please hold onto your questions for just a little while."

    She proceeds to stand over you and holds her hands above your chest. She says words. But what she says makes zero sense to you, almost as if she is speaking gibberish.

    And like so much else since you woke up, what happens next is supposed to only be possible in your imagination. A slight orange glow seems to eminate from the space between your chest and her hands.

    <<button [[Continue | WakingUp3]]>><</button>>

:: WakingUp3
    <img src="img/medicalwing.jpg" alt="medical wing photo"/>

    $npcs.Amy.formal notices your wide eyed stare.

    "I know, more questions. And truely, I would love to answer them all! I really do. But like I said, not my place."

    With a wide smile, she says "The good news is you are as healthy and whole as when you first arrived here. Tell me, how are you feeling, aside from lost and confused?"

    <<button [[Lost and confused sums it up | WakingUp4]]>><<relGain Amy 5>><</button>>
    <<button [[Just tell me something! | WakingUp4]]>><<relGain Amy -5>><</button>>
    <<button [[I am fine. Thank you. | WakingUp4]]>><<relGain Amy 10>><</button>>

:: WakingUp4
    <img src="img/medicalwing.jpg" alt="medical wing photo"/>\
    <<printRelGain>>\

    $npcs.Amy.formal says comfortingly, "Oh there there, I wouldn't worry. We all have our parts to play." With a wink and a smile she says "Give me a moment and I will have someone take you to the headmaster."

    You see her wave her hands around in a series of small circular motions while speaking gibberish again. Suddenly, a barely visible, transparent blue orb appears in front of her and floats out of the room and through the closed door.

    With you brain fog still in full force, you are as perplexed as ever. A few seconds later a woman opens the large wooden doors to to the room. She briefly looks at you before speaking with $npcs.Amy.formal.

    "You called for me $npcs.Amy.title? I assume this one is ready to meet with the headmaster?"

    $npcs.Amy.formal replies, "Good evening, $npcs.Janessa.formal. And yes, all set."

    $npcs.Amy.formal looks at you and says, "This is $npcs.Janessa.firstName, she will show you the way to the headmaster's study. Let me know if your daze sticks with you for more than a day or two. And if you have any other medical needs, just come see me here in the Medical Wing."

    With a hint of concern and something akin to sadness or pity, she says, "Please, take care of yourself."

    $npcs.Amy.formal walks over to $npcs.Janessa.firstName and speaks with her quietely. You cannot hear what either one is saying, but $npcs.Janessa.firstName appears annoyed by whatever it is.

    $npcs.Janessa.firstName looks at you and says, "Come on."

    For the first time since you woke up, you roll onto your side and place your bare feet on the cold slate floor. You notice that the thin, bright red gown you are wearing is definitely not yours. At least it covers all the important bits.

    When stop looking at the strange outfit you are wearing (and pushing aside the question of who undressed and redressed you), you notice a mirror next to the headboard of the bed. Your first glance suprises you. You look...different.

    At least you still remember your name,
    <<textbox "$plrName.fName" "First">> \
    <<textbox "$plrName.lName" "Last">>

